[l_english.STATE_LORE_60]
Nan Du, meaning “the capital in the south” in Kirinese, was once a prosperous city-state built by one or even several generations of Kirins in some unknown number of cycles ago. Their fate was easy to predict: the city-state that eventually turned into ashes, devoured by the Nirik flames, and the survivors migrated either westward, eastward, or northward.
Legend has it that the newly established Kirin civilization on the western coast had a prolonged conflict with the civilization in the south that had already turned into Niriks, resulting in many ancient battlefield ruins and mythological legends. For example, Hei Sha Fu, meaning “the city-state in the black desert”, describes a city-state devoured by flames on the battlefield between the two civilizations in the east and west. It was named after the land that was scorched black by the war. For example, Bei Sai and Nan Sai, meaning “the fortress in the north” and “the fortress in the south” in Kirinese, were military fortresses established by the west to resist the Nirik invasion from Nan Du, which later developed into towns.
Historians also speculate that the Great Moat was built during this period — the Kirin civilization mobilized almost all of its labor to draw water from the oasis, dig a great moat running north and south, to resist the flames from the east. However, by the time the moat that exhausted the country’s resources was completed, the civilization in the west had already gone through countless cycles.

[l_simp_chinese.STATE_LORE_60]
南都，麒麟语中“南方的首都”之意。在不知多少个轮回以前，一代，甚至可能是几代麒麟的文明曾在这里建立过繁荣的城邦。他们的结局并不意外，最终逆麟化的城邦在烈焰中化作尘埃，幸存者向西、向东或向北迁徙。
传说中，在西部沿海新建立的麒麟文明曾与南部已经逆麟化的文明曾爆发过持续的冲突，由此产生了许多古战场遗迹与神话传说。例如，黑沙府，麒麟语中“黑色沙漠中的城邦”，就是描述的一个在东西两个文明的战场中被烈焰吞噬的城邦，因土地都因为战火烧焦成黑色而得名。再比如，北塞与南塞，麒麟语中“北方的要塞”与“南方的要塞”，就是西方在抵御南都的逆麟入侵时建立的军事要塞，后来发展为城镇。
还有历史学家推测，“长河”也是在这一时期修建的——麒麟文明动用了几乎全部的劳动力，引绿洲之水，开凿了一条纵贯南北的大河，用以抵御东方的烈火。不过当那条耗尽全国资源的河流完工之时，西部的文明也已经不知道走过了多少个轮回。
